{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Base Point of a Parametrization.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Base Point of a Parametrization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"base point of a parametrization base point of a parametrization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Base Point of a Parametrization.md","fileName":"Base Point of a Parametrization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Base Point of a Parametrization","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 20:15\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Regular Sequences and Syzygies]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Base Point of a Parametrization.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Base Point of a Parametrization.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"base point of a parametrization base point of a parametrization","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Base Point of a Parametrization.md","fileName":"Base Point of a Parametrization.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Base Point of a Parametrization","heading":"Base Point of a Parametrization","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A base point of a projective parametrization is a parameter value at which every defining homogeneous polynomial vanishes. The coordinate formulas therefore fail to determine an image point there.\n\nBase points carry algebraic and geometric multiplicities. Their contributions reduce the degree of a generically one-to-one parametrized surface from the square of the polynomial degree, linking local intersection data to global implicit geometry.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Regular Sequences and Syzygies","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Base Point of a Parametrization.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - F